** large-slip pull-out of a bar tilted by 45 degrees to a structured mesh, running through its nodes and along the
** diagonals of its elements (the edge case of the partner search); regression test, the response equals the one of a
** bar aligned with the mesh (pytest test_large_slip_pull_out_does_not_depend_on_the_orientation)
** concrete block 200 x 200 (CPE8R 10 x 10, plane strain section, thickness 150), Ø16 bar along y = x - 40 with a
** bonded length of 120 mm and a free length of 20 mm (one bar element: a truss has no transverse stiffness without
** tension, so free interior nodes would be a mechanism at the start), exiting through the loaded face x = 200, which
** bears on a plate; the bar is pulled 30 mm along its axis, completely out; units N, mm
